0..75 Comment "// A constructor at a type that a definition computes names its own family."
76..153 Comment "// `pairOf(Nat, Nat)` unfolds to `Both(Nat, Nat)`, and `MkBoth` checks there."
154..156 Comment "//"
157..232 Comment "// The type the constructor is checked at names no family. The printer must"
233..293 Comment "// still write the declaration back as the source writes it."
294..296 Comment "//"
297..373 Comment "// The printer spells the constructor by the family on its node. The fixture"
374..447 Comment "// that refuses a constructor of one family under a classifier of another"
448..499 Comment "// family is the pathological twin of this fixture."
500..502 Comment "//"
503..544 Comment "// - see: #3669 — `bothZero`, `bothOne`"
545..601 Comment "// - see: `pathological/data/nominal-distinctness.gandr`"
